{"id":"sample_points_by_radius","compound_name":"Graphs::Geometry_Queries::sample_points_by_radius","source_path":"sample_points_by_radius/sample_points_by_radius.json","category":"Geometry Queries","author":"Autodesk","description":"This example demonstrates weighted sampling between points and a plane","documentation_file":"sample_points_by_radius_docs_ENU.md","documentation":"## Sample Points By Radius\n\n### What it does\n\nThis graph demonstrates `sample_points_by_radius`.  \n\n### Inputs and outputs\n\nThe inputs for this graph are a plane of coloured points, displayed as cubes, a ground plane geometry to sample from and a time compound to provide animation.\n\n### How it works\n\nFor every *position* input it will search within a *radius* for points in the `geometry` and return a *weighted average* of the property by the distance to the samples.\n\nInside nested iterate/for each loops, the property is sampled and a *weight* is calculated based on the points inside radius provided.  The original value is them multiplied by this generated weight and returned.\n\nFor example, if a position samples 4 points in a given radius then it will average the property at those 4 points based on the distance to those points.","library_dependencies":{"Amino":"2.15.0.9","bif":"2.15.0.9"},"graph_ports":[{"portName":"out_points1","portDirection":"output","portType":"Object"},{"portName":"geometry_with_material1","portDirection":"output","portType":"Object"}],"terminal_states":[],"counts":{"nodes":17,"connections":26,"values":27,"compounds":2},"node_types":{"Modeling::Primitive::create_mesh_plane":2,"Geometry::Properties::get_point_position":2,"Diagnostic::Display::assign_diagnostic_material":2,"Geometry::Query::sample_points_by_radius":1,"Value::string":1,"Geometry::Properties::set_point_shape":1,"Core::Time::time":1,"colored_plane_of_points":1,"Core::Graph::pass":1,"Core::FCurve::evaluate_fcurve":1,"Core::Array::array_bounds":1,"Core::Math::change_range":1,"Geometry::Points::c